{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1563299-taste-of-blood-trained-observer","id":1563299,"title":"Taste of Blood - Trained Observer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-20T23:17:14-07:00","id":1563299,"title":"Taste of Blood - Trained Observer","content":"Good day<br /> <br /> Just a quick question - could you apply the 8/9-Again buff from Trained Observer while using Taste of Blood. <br /> <br /> Taste of Blood is, in essence, a perception roll, However, Trained Observer is a human merit, not a vampire merit. So I am torn.<br /> <br /> What say you all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24245-ruggedrock","name":"ruggedrock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T00:23:59-07:00","id":1563300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ruggedrock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1563299-taste-of-blood-trained-observer#post1563299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good day<br /> <br /> Just a quick question - could you apply the 8/9-Again buff from Trained Observer while using Taste of Blood.<br /> <br /> Taste of Blood is, in essence, a perception roll, However, Trained Observer is a human merit, not a vampire merit. So I am torn.<br /> <br /> What say you all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some precedent to kindred analogs of human merits being developed/manifested by particular individuals from time to time.<br /> The Kindred Medium merit in City of the Damned: New Orleans is an example that easily comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T07:13:46-07:00","id":1563303,"title":"","content":"I would say &quot;no&quot; not because Trained Observer is a human Merit, but because Taste of Blood is not actually a Perception roll \u2014 using Wits + Composure is not enough to qualify for the benefit, else it would also apply to Reaction To Surprise rolls or simply say it applies to Wits rolls to perceive details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T10:06:49-07:00","id":1563308,"title":"","content":"Maybe. My instinct is to say no, as It feels a bit too different to what the merit seems to describe.<br /> <br /> But then I think it might depend on how you conceptualise tasting blood. Like, is it a deliberate action, kinda like wine tasting, (as I first thought) or is it a more instinctual thing which might more realistically benefit from the merit.<br /> <br /> It's also a somewhat niche issue, so I don't think it'd a huge problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T11:03:56-07:00","id":1563309,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I was about to echo what others have already said, but upon researching inside both CoD and VTR 2<sup>e,</sup> I cannot find where Perception is clearly defined outside of a simple Wits + Composure roll on page 163. Let\u2019s look at all the relevant information I could find inside the core book.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VTR P.170</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Attribute Tasks</b><br /> Some actions require no special expertise to perform. Mostly, these come in the form of Wits + Composure rolls to notice somehting that doesn\u2019t seem right, or using Strength + Stamina rolls to lift something. In these rolls, you add two different Attributes together to make your dice pool. If an action doesn\u2019t seem to involve any particular skill, it can be handled by an attribute task.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VTR P.91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A taste of Blood</b><br /> In addition to being able to smell blood and to identify and track with blood, Kindred can discern cues from blood they taste.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> VTR P.124</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Trained observer</b><br /> Your character has spent years in the field, catching tiny details and digging for secrets. She might not have a better chance at finding things, but she has a better chance of finding <i>important</i> things. Any time you make a Perception roll (usually Wits + Composure) you benefit from the 9-again quality. With the three-dot version, you get 8-again.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Given that :</b></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I can\u2019t find any <i>specific </i>perception action clearly defined beyond \u2018\u2019Wits + Compsure\u2019\u2019.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Tasting definitely enters the realm of perception.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">The merit specifies that it\u2019s design to help in finding extra details.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Exceptional successes on Taste of Blood grant extra insight.</span></li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>I conclude that :</b> It should apply.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">It\u2019s not especially powerful either. As Michael has mentioned, it\u2019s pretty niche.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T12:53:44-07:00","id":1563312,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26771_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26771\" data-vbnamecard=\"26771\">Algarik</a> There's one other piece. The <i>CofD</i> core has a negative description of Perception rolls under the Investigation skill on page 33:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using this Skill [Investigation] is different that the Perception Attribute task that can be found under Wits and Composure. Perception is typically checked when a character is not actively searching, but can potentially see something out of place of unusual. </div> </div> </div>That's what swings me towards allowing it if we conceptualise blood tasting as a passive ability rather than a practiced ability.<br /> <br /> There's also page 45 of the 1e core, which details what Perception rolls are. It's the previous edition but I think a lot of 2e was written with the assumption that you know 1e relatively well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T14:21:37-07:00","id":1563315,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> Ah good catch, i missed that one in CoD.<br /> <br /> It doesn't change my analysis for 2nd specifically. The game lacks a clearly defined task called ''perception''.<br /> <br /> I went and also reread Kindred Senses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VTR P.91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any of her Kindred Senses apply, add her Blood Potency to any rolls to detect hidden people or details by the traces of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trained observer would definitely apply to any perception roll boosted by Blood Potency and Taste of Blood is a side bar of Kindred Senses.<br /> <br /> I managed to find the 1st-ed description. If we use 1st ed version, it might weaken my claim however.<br /> <br /> Indeed, since ''Perception'' is its own task, then one could make the argument that trained observer only applies to perception task roll.<br /> <br /> In the end, since Taste of Blood is indeed Wits + Composure it seems like it's not something you can truly train unlike a skill, thus it would support your ''passive ability'' claim.<br /> <br /> I personally still lean on letting it fly for multiple reasons:<br /> 1. Taste of Blood is niche.<br /> 2. Trained observer would already apply with kindred senses.<br /> 3. The merit is printed in VTR 2e, so it's not like it wasn't intended for vampire to have.<br /> 4. Personally think it's cooler to have expert blood taster on a domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T19:46:27-07:00","id":1563325,"title":"","content":"While I disagree with defining &quot;perception&quot; just by being Wits + Composure, I think Taste of Blood definitely qualifies as a perception task by its own context.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of it applying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T01:29:57-07:00","id":1564162,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have my books at the moment but I\u2019m leaning towards allowing it. From what I remember the Taste of Blood drawback activates on a dramatic success which if right would make allowing them to work together risky for the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}